    <innerclass refid="structWouldBlock" prot="public">WouldBlock</innerclass>
    <innerclass refid="classDbProbe" prot="public">DbProbe</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Control-flow signal that a request needs the database and must move off the IO thread. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header defines two pieces of the IO-thread fast path: <ref refid="structWouldBlock" kindref="compound">WouldBlock</ref>, a small exception-like signal that is deliberately not a std::exception, and <ref refid="classDbProbe" kindref="compound">DbProbe</ref>, an RAII marker that sets a thread-local &quot;probing&quot; flag for its lifetime. While the flag is set, <ref refid="classDbProbe_1af3b9ebe61addb4dd1885a3d117221a1f" kindref="member">DbProbe::check()</ref> throws <ref refid="structWouldBlock" kindref="compound">WouldBlock</ref> so that any code about to touch the database stops before it does any work or writes a response.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: It lets simple requests finish without the cost of queueing onto the DB executor. The HTTP wrapper creates a <ref refid="classDbProbe" kindref="compound">DbProbe</ref> on the IO thread and runs the controller once; requests answered from memory (bad JSON, cached permission denial) complete there. The first operation that needs a connection calls check(), throws <ref refid="structWouldBlock" kindref="compound">WouldBlock</ref>, and the wrapper re-runs the whole request on a DB worker where no probe is active. <ref refid="structWouldBlock" kindref="compound">WouldBlock</ref> is not a std::exception on purpose, so generic error handlers do not swallow this control-flow signal. Without it, every request would pay the queueing cost even when no database access was needed.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>RAII (a flag set in the constructor and cleared in the destructor): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/raii">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/raii</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>thread_local storage (one variable instance per thread): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/storage_duration">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/storage_duration</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Control-flow exceptions (throwing to change execution path, not to report an error)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Exceptions that do not derive from std::exception: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/exception">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/exception</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>static inline members: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/static">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/static</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
